## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your Unity project's `Assets/`.
{% if s.input_backend == "input_system" %}
2. Drop `Input/{{ s.name }}.inputactions` into `Assets/` and install the **Input System** package
   (`com.unity.inputsystem`) if it isn't already installed.
{% endif %}
3. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to any GameObject you want the player to control.
{% if variant == "multi_mode" %}
4. Builds every registered mode's rig on Awake (`CharacterController` for
   on_foot, a 4-wheel `WheelCollider` rig for vehicle_car) — both exist on the
   GameObject at once, only one enabled at a time. Press **{{ s.mode_switch_key }}**
   to cycle modes (`CycleMode()`/`SwitchMode(kind)` are also callable directly).

**Control Surface Stack — known v1 limitations** (see docs/CONTROL_SURFACE_STACK.md):
- No velocity/momentum carries across a mode switch — `SwitchMode` zeroes it.
- One spatial layout for the whole project (the *starting* mode's — see
  `select_archetype` in `src/unity_layout_archetype.py`), not one per mode.
- The camera and animator subsystems are tuned for the starting mode only,
  not re-tuned per mode.
- Mode registry: {{ s.modes | map(attribute='kind') | join(', ') }}
  (default: `{{ s.default_mode }}`)
{% elif variant == "vehicle_hover" %}
4. Builds a raycast spring-damper hover rig on Awake (no WheelColliders — for
   craft with no wheel bones). `Rigidbody` + collider are added automatically if missing.
{% elif variant.startswith("vehicle_") %}
4. Builds a 4-wheel `WheelCollider` rig on Awake (uses named wheel bones if the
   model has them, primitive wheels otherwise). `Rigidbody` + collider are added
   automatically if missing.
{% elif variant.startswith("2d_") %}
4. Requires `Rigidbody2D` + a 2D collider on the controlled object.
{% else %}
4. The `CharacterController` will be added automatically on Awake if missing.
{% endif %}

